From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Oliver Sargison <sargo@sargo.cc>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +1300
Subject: [PATCH 01/13] Plutonium: the shell page and the window broker, in the
 browser

The shell page (--plutonium-shell-origin, --plutonium-shell-url) and what makes it the desktop: the window broker and its grants (ExoWindowBroker), the embedder that puts Exo's windows into the page, several shells at once, tags and groups, keys the shell takes, and the agent bridge's browser side.

It holds these changes:
- native fullscreen for embedded apps and tabs, Super+F, shell shortcuts
- several live shells, Super+Tab switches between them
- windowrequest events, and which element drives a window
- unit tests for the broker and grant checks

and the parts in these files of:
- Exo embedding (Phase 1) and window broker (Phase 2)
- report Wayland client pid through the window broker
- windowBroker.showOnDesktop to pop an embedded window out
- windowBroker.close() and snapshot() for the agent bridge
- shell mode on DRM, evdev input fix, display-plane path
- browser tabs as SurfaceEmbed elements, DRM mouse wheel
- tab automation over DevTools, SurfaceEmbed fixes
- pointer capture (lock, confine) for embedded apps, Super+Escape
- tags and groups on windows and tabs, the Super+Tab overlay
- niri shell keys, touchpad and scrolling, drag and drop, shell links as tabs
- object-fit and a resize cross-fade for <native-window>
- Chrome's own UI in the shell (DevTools, context menus, keys)
- the switcher: shell pages, fullscreen windows, backup terminal and browser
- Google sign-in on the web; tabs fullscreen outside the shells
- agents drive windows and tabs over DevTools
- broker follow-ups: grantrevoked, unsubscribing, NativeWindowEvent constructor
- common plumbing for tab features
- page zoom for tabs
- find in page for tabs
- tabs' permission prompts ask the shell
- per-thread permission grants
- downloads for the shells' tabs
- file pickers for tabs ask the shell
- printing in tabs goes to the shell
- a parked window's popups show only where a page shows it
- incognito tabs, each in a throwaway off-the-record profile
- screen capture for shells, capture requests to the focused shell
- PipeWire video nodes for captures, getDisplayMedia asks the shell
- several displays, a shell per display, one window in one place
- dmabufs for PipeWire consumers that import them
- ext-image-copy-capture-v1 in Exo, for grim
- pages see Linux, not ChromeOS
- an app's interactive move or resize hands the drag to the page
- xdg_activation_v1, apps raise their windows through the shell
- the switcher's installed shells: an exact list from the launcher, customizing and server controls on a shell's page
- the lock screen and idle: Ash's own lock over every display, Super+L, the idle time, the wake locks and the displays' power in the Plutonium domain
- touchpad swipes with three fingers or more go to the shell page
- only the shell window is held fullscreen
- windowBroker.getHelperUrl()
- xdg_toplevel_icon_v1, apps' window icons for the shells
- a floating native window keeps its client-side resize edges
- tabs' media sessions over MPRIS
- speechSynthesis voices from speech-dispatcher
- desktop settings and a display configuration tool in the switcher
